The configure script should check for all these libs, but nevertheless here is
a list of the dependencies.

Requirements:

- libgtkmm >= 4.0

- libglibmm >= 2.68

- gstreamer >= 1.0

- libxml++ >= 5.0
        an XML parser.  Found at: http://libxmlplusplus.sourceforge.net

- libarchive >= 0.28
        a library for managing tar files.  Found at: http:/www.libarchive.org

- libsigc++ >= 3.0
	Found at http://libsigc.sf.net

- libxslt >= 1.1.20
        Found at http://xmlsoft.org/

- pkg-config
        Generally distributed with the Linux distribution.

- GNU gettext 
        Generally distributed with the Linux distribution.


on Ubuntu you need the following packages:
sudo apt-get install automake autoconf libtool m4 autotools-dev autopoint g++ libsigc++-2.0-dev libglibmm-2.4-dev libgtkmm-4.0-dev gettext git libgstreamer-1.0-dev intltool libarchive-dev libxslt1-dev libxml++5.0-dev

on Fedora you need the following packages:
sudo dnf install gtkmm4.0-devel gettext gstreamer1-devel libxml++50-devel libsigc++30-devel intltool automake autoconf m4 git libarchive-devel libxslt-devel gcc-c++ libtool

Please report changes in these package installation commands if they fail to work for you.  Use the bug-tracker at https://sv.nongnu.org/bugs/?group=lordsawar.
